## Context

Author's ruling 2026-09-23 (`DECISIONS.md`): a sitter build climbs five rungs —
unit, smoke, Menagerie, clone, dogfood — and is released only after the author
has used it himself. The ladder itself is written once, in
`plugins/sdt-sitter/TESTING.md`; this ticket tracks the work that makes each
rung real.

## Children

- 0816 — the integrity check, rung 2 and up
- 0817 — the Menagerie rung, lifecycle folded into its scenario (itself a
  tracker: 0820 rename, 0821 whole corpus, 0822 lifecycle)
- 0818 — the clone rung
- 0819 — the bar for rung 3 and above
- 0794 — the two wild documents the Menagerie lacks, without which rung 3 is
  not the wild rung the ruling makes it

## Exit criteria

Every child closed, and one build — the first after the children land — has
climbed rungs 1 to 4 with each verdict recorded in the rung record directory
and the integrity check green at each rung that has one. Integration review per
the tracker rule before closing.
